Decode a Hextile rectangle into the current framebuffer.

Start without a background or foreground color. Visit tiles left to right and
top to bottom. Limit each tile to sixteen pixels per side and shorten tiles at
the right and bottom edges of the rectangle.

For a raw tile, read opaque pixels and clear both carried colors. For a color
tile, validate the flags. Read a new background or reuse a valid prior one.
Read a new foreground when supplied. Clear the carried foreground when each
subrectangle supplies its own color. Fill the tile with the background.

When a tile supplies subrectangles, read their count and decode each position
and size. Use the specified pixel or the valid foreground. Check each rectangle
against the actual tile bounds and subtract its area from the update paint
budget before painting. Reject invalid flags, missing colors, truncated data,
out-of-bounds geometry, or budget exhaustion before publishing the update.
